ABSTRACT
================================================================================

The Hodge Complex Standard Model derives the hypercharge functional on the
15-dimensional sector-coarse space of the 14-mode multiplet at lambda = 4
(HCSM-07). This paper proves that the resulting hypercharge functional is
anomaly-free. On the HCSM state content (Input 1, the Standard Model
content per generation), the four one-loop anomaly conditions

    Tr(Y) = 0,  Tr(Y^3) = 0,  SU(2)^2 U(1) = 0,  SU(3)^2 U(1) = 0

vanish identically in rational arithmetic. The three cubic gauge anomalies
SU(3)^3, SU(2)^3, and the mixed SU(3)-SU(2)-U(1) vanish by the structure of
the Standard Model content. The Witten global SU(2) anomaly is evaded
because each generation carries an even number of SU(2) doublets. Two-loop
anomaly cancellation is automatic by the Adler-Bardeen theorem. In the
sector-coarse framing, the mixed SU(3)^2 U(1) condition reduces to the
weighted sector identity Y_0 + 2 Y_1 + Y_2 = 0, which is satisfied by the
HCSM hypercharge coefficients (-2/3, +1/6, +1/3) on the A_1 block. The
anomaly cancellation is a consistency theorem of the HCSM structure:
conditional on the Standard Model content (Input 1) and the physical
identification of the A_1 isotypic with color and B_1 with weak isospin
(Input 2), the HCSM hypercharge functional is uniquely determined by
HCSM-07 and is automatically anomaly-free. All claims are HCSM-native and
verified at machine precision.


