1.1 The anomaly cancellation problem
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Hodge Complex Standard Model (HCSM) derives the gauge algebra
su(3) + su(2) + u(1)^5 as a Lie subalgebra of the D4 commutant on the
14-mode multiplet at lambda = 4 (HCSM-06 [HCSM-06]). On the full
56-dimensional Hodge sector, the hypercharge functional is a specific
element of the 15-dimensional sector-coarse space (HCSM-07 [HCSM-07]):

    Y = sum_rho (alpha_rho I + beta_rho F + gamma_rho O) P_rho,      (1)

with coefficients for the A_1 and B_1 blocks uniquely determined by the
Standard Model content and the sector assignment:

    (alpha_{A_1}, beta_{A_1}, gamma_{A_1}) = (0, -1/6, -1/2),        (2)

    (alpha_{B_1}, beta_{B_1}, gamma_{B_1}) = (0, +1/2, +1/2).        (3)

A gauge theory with chiral fermions is consistent only if its anomaly
coefficients vanish. This paper proves that the HCSM hypercharge
functional (1) satisfies this consistency condition.

The paper is a theorem: given the Standard Model content (Input 1) and
the HCSM hypercharge functional (HCSM-07), the four one-loop anomaly
conditions vanish identically in rational arithmetic. Two-loop
cancellation follows from Adler-Bardeen, and the Witten global anomaly
is evaded by the even number of doublets per generation.

1.2 The one-line summary
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    The HCSM hypercharge functional, uniquely determined by the
    sector-coarse space and the Standard Model content, is anomaly-free.
    The four one-loop conditions Tr(Y), Tr(Y^3), SU(2)^2 U(1), and
    SU(3)^2 U(1) vanish exactly in rational arithmetic. The three cubic
    gauge anomalies vanish by the structure of the content. The Witten
    global SU(2) anomaly is evaded. Two-loop cancellation is automatic
    by Adler-Bardeen.

