2.1 The state content
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Standard Model content per generation, in left-handed convention
(Input 1 of HCSM-06 [HCSM-06] and HCSM-07 [HCSM-07]), is

    Q_L(3, 2, +1/6) x 6,  u_R^c (3, 1, -2/3) x 3,
    d_R^c (3, 1, +1/3) x 3,                                          (4)

    L_L (1, 2, -1/2) x 2,  e_R^c (1, 1, +1) x 1,
    nu_R^c (1, 1, 0) x 1.                                            (5)

Here the notation is X(SU(3), SU(2), Y) x n with n the multiplicity.

The content is realized on the HCSM state space as follows:

  - The color-triplet states u_R^c, Q_L, d_R^c occupy the A_1 multiplicity
    space of the 56-dimensional Hodge sector at lambda = 4 (HCSM-06).
  - The weak-doublet states Q_L, L_L occupy the B_1 multiplicity space.
  - The hypercharge values are the HCSM hypercharge functional evaluated
    on the corresponding sector (HCSM-07).

2.2 The HCSM hypercharge values
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

By HCSM-07 [HCSM-07], the hypercharge functional has the sector values

    Y_{A_1}: (Omega^0, Omega^1, Omega^2)
        = (-2/3, +1/6, +1/3),                                        (6)

    Y_{B_1}: (Omega^0, Omega^1, Omega^2)
        = (+1, -1/2, 0).                                             (7)

These are the values assigned to the HCSM sectors, matching the Standard
Model content (4)-(5) under Input 3 (sector assignment) of HCSM-07.

Remark (Sector-coarse reading of (4)-(5)). The four multiplets
u_R^c, Q_L, d_R^c (color-triplet) are assigned to the three Hodge sectors
Omega^0, Omega^1, Omega^2 respectively. The three multiplets
e_R^c, L_L, nu_R^c (leptons) carry the B_1 hypercharge values
+1, -1/2, 0 on the same three sectors.

2.3 The four one-loop anomaly conditions
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The four one-loop anomaly conditions for a
SU(3)_c x SU(2)_L x U(1)_Y chiral gauge theory are

    Tr(Y) = 0,                            (linear/gravitational),    (8)

    Tr(Y^3) = 0,                          (cubic U(1)),              (9)

    SU(2)^2 U(1) = 0,                     (mixed electroweak),       (10)

    SU(3)^2 U(1) = 0,                     (mixed color).             (11)

The traces run over the chiral fermion content per generation. With the
content (4)-(5), each condition is a rational-arithmetic sum that must
vanish for the theory to be consistent.

2.4 The three cubic gauge anomalies
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The cubic gauge anomalies are

    SU(3)^3,  SU(2)^3,  SU(3)-SU(2)-U(1).                            (12)

These vanish by the structure of the Standard Model content and the
safety of the gauge groups, as established in Section 7.


