11.2 Inputs
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Input 1 (Standard Model content). The per-generation content (4)-(5),
including the specific hypercharge values -2/3, +1/6, +1/3, -1/2, +1, 0.
This input is shared with HCSM-06 and HCSM-07.

Input 2 (physical identification). The identification of the A_1 factor
with physical color and the B_1 factor with physical weak isospin
(HCSM-06 [HCSM-06]).

Input 3 (sector assignment). The assignment of u_R^c, Q_L, d_R^c to the
Hodge sectors Omega^0, Omega^1, Omega^2 (HCSM-07 [HCSM-07]).

Universal tools. The Dynkin indices T(2) = T(3) = 1/2 for the fundamental
representations of SU(2) and SU(3), the Adler-Bardeen theorem, and the
Witten global SU(2) anomaly criterion. These are standard mathematical
and physics facts, not framework inputs.

11.3 What is not claimed
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

We do not claim to derive the Standard Model content or the specific
hypercharge values from first principles. These are Input 1. The
framework derives that, given this content and the HCSM hypercharge
functional, the resulting theory is anomaly-free.

The framework's claim is: the HCSM hypercharge functional, uniquely
determined by the sector-coarse space and the Standard Model content, is
anomaly-free. This is a consistency theorem of the HCSM structure: the
HCSM hypercharge values satisfy all known anomaly cancellation
conditions.


