13. CONCLUSION
================================================================================

This paper has established that the HCSM hypercharge functional is
anomaly-free.

The four one-loop anomaly conditions

    Tr(Y) = 0,  Tr(Y^3) = 0,
    SU(2)^2 U(1) = 0,  SU(3)^2 U(1) = 0

vanish identically in rational arithmetic on the Standard Model content
per generation, with hypercharge values given by the HCSM sector-coarse
functional (HCSM-07 [HCSM-07]). The three cubic gauge anomalies SU(3)^3,
SU(2)^3, SU(3)-SU(2)-U(1) vanish by the structure of the content. The
Witten global SU(2) anomaly is evaded because each generation carries 4
SU(2) doublets (an even number). Two-loop cancellation is automatic by
the Adler-Bardeen theorem.

In the sector-coarse framing, the mixed SU(3)^2 U(1) condition reduces to
the weighted sector identity

    Y(Omega^0) + 2 Y(Omega^1) + Y(Omega^2) = 0,

which is satisfied by the HCSM hypercharge values (-2/3, +1/6, +1/3) on
the A_1 block. The weight 2 on the middle sector reflects the weak-doublet
content hosted there.

The anomaly cancellation is a consistency theorem of the HCSM structure.
Given the Standard Model content (Input 1), the physical identification
of the A_1 isotypic with color and B_1 with weak isospin (Input 2), and
the sector assignment of the color-triplet multiplets (Input 3), the HCSM
hypercharge functional is uniquely determined by HCSM-07 and is
automatically anomaly-free. The framework's claim is: the HCSM hypercharge
functional is the unique anomaly-free functional compatible with the
sector-coarse structure and the Standard Model content.


