DC.description: The Hodge Complex Standard Model derives the hypercharge
  functional on the 15-dimensional sector-coarse space of the 14-mode
  multiplet at lambda = 4. This paper proves that the resulting
  hypercharge functional is anomaly-free: the four one-loop conditions
  Tr(Y), Tr(Y^3), SU(2)^2 U(1), SU(3)^2 U(1) vanish identically in
  rational arithmetic; the cubic gauge anomalies vanish by content
  structure; the Witten global anomaly is evaded by the even number of
  doublets per generation; two-loop cancellation is automatic by
  Adler-Bardeen. In the sector-coarse framing, the mixed SU(3)^2 U(1)
  condition reduces to the weighted sector identity Y_0 + 2 Y_1 + Y_2 = 0.
